eral-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Jeff Van Drew (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Incumbent Jeff Van Drew seeks another term in a South Jersey district that leans Republican by about five points. He has out-raised Democratic nominee Zack Mullock roughly four to one and holds a large cash advantage, with no significant outside spending reported on either side. Expert ratings mostly place the race in the Likely or Solid Republican column, though one outlet calls it a Tossup.\n\nPublic polling is nearly nonexistent: the only survey is a year-old Democratic-sponsored poll showing Van Drew ahead by ten. Prediction markets give Mullock roughly a one-in-five chance. The race appears likely to stay with the incumbent, with modest but real room for a Democratic upset if the national environment breaks hard against Republicans.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1228, "margin": -7.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1056, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0906, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0722, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1002, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1154, "margin": -8.0}]}